      why: "The US and EU tables are the same. With LVEF above 45 per cent and a fall of 10 to 20 points, or LVEF of 40 to 45 per cent and a fall of less than 10 points, treatment continues, with a repeat scan within 3 weeks in the second case. After an interruption for LVEF of 40 to 45 per cent with a fall of 10 to 20 points, treatment resumes at the same dose if LVEF recovers to within 10 per cent from baseline, in the label's words, and is stopped for good if it does not. Unlike the trastuzumab labels, neither text sets a scan interval: both say at regular intervals as clinically indicated.",
      source: "us-enhertu",
