      why: "The US and EU tables match on these numbers. The US table has a row the EU table does not: stop for good for confirmed symptomatic congestive heart failure. The EU SmPC says that if LVEF declines and has not improved, or has declined further at the next assessment, zanidatamab should be discontinued as its table recommends. The US label says the safety of zanidatamab has not been established in people whose baseline ejection fraction is below 50 per cent.",
